      "t": "Automattic debuts a platform to deploy vibe-coding apps amid a changing internet",
      "d": "Automattic aims to compete with the likes of Lovable with Spacefast.",
      "u": "https://techcrunch.com/2026/11/09/automattic-debuts-a-platform-to-deploy-vibe-coding-apps-amid-a-changing-internet/",
      "m": "11. 09. PM 02:00",
      "ts": 1794232800000,
      "fullText": "WordPress has been a crucial technology and content management system for websites like TechCrunch. Now, WordPress.com owner Automattic is responding to the changing state of the web by debuting a new service called Spacefast , which will allow users to deploy vibe-coded websites and apps. Spacefast is designed to provide infrastructure for the vibe-coded apps, including databases, authentication, file uploads, emails, and analytics, to make them functional websites, apps, or services. The product competes with the likes of Lovable and Emergent, which offer both interface and rails for vibe-coded apps, but in a more open way. Users can connect Spacefast with other agents and chatbots like ChatGPT, Claude, Hermes, OpenClaw, Grok Bot, Muse, Pi, Cursor, OpenCode, and Amp. Alternatively, they can connect a Git repository to Spacefast to get started. The product is headed by Batuhan İçöz, who worked on it during one of the company&#8217;s hackathon sprints earlier in the year. At that time, he worked on the company&#8217;s cross-platform messaging app Beeper and said that he often got Vercel links from his non-technical friends while exploring vibe coding. &#8220;I thought there had to be a better way for everyone to set up and deploy their projects. Automattic already has good infrastructure, but we have been traditionally associated with just WordPress. I thought, why do I have to use Cloudflare when we have a CDN (content delivery network) just as good? So I started working on what was called Stattic and now Spacefast,&#8221; he told TechCrunch over a call. An Office-themed game on Spacefast Image Credits: Spacefast İçöz eventually disseminated the solution to his friends and added more features to make the product more dynamic. Automattic soft-launched the product in September to get feedback before today&#8217;s launch. The company has seen varied use cases of their product, with people and organizations using it for internal mockups, slideshows, and offer-related w"
